text:
JWT `exp` in seconds. `Date.now()` in milliseconds.

**Bug:**
```js
if (Date.now() > decoded.exp) // wrong — always true, exp looks ancient
```

**Fix:**
```js
if (Date.now() / 1000 > decoded.exp) // convert ms → s
// or
if (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > decoded.exp)
```

**Better:** ditch manual check, let `jsonwebtoken` handle it:
```js
jwt.verify(token, secret, (err, decoded) => {
  if (err) return res.status(401).json({ error: err.message });
  // TokenExpiredError thrown automatically
  next();
});
```

`verify()` reject expired tokens, throw `TokenExpiredError`. No manual `exp` math needed.
